            "answer": 1,
            "explain": "The de Rham pairing $\\Omega^k(M)\\times C_k(M)\\to\\mathbb{R}$, $(\\omega,\\sigma)\\mapsto\\int_\\sigma\\omega$, descends to a perfect pairing of cohomology with real homology by Stokes's theorem. The induced map $H^k_{\\mathrm{dR}}\\to H^k(M;\\mathbb{R})$ is an isomorphism."
