            "answer": 1,
            "explain": "Units satisfy $|N_{K/\\mathbb{Q}}(u)|=1$. Taking logarithms, $\\sum_i\\log|\\sigma_i(u)|+\\sum_j\\log|\\tau_j(u)|^2=\\log|N(u)|=0$. The complex coordinates carry weight $2$ exactly because each complex place $\\tau_j$ contributes $|\\tau_j(u)|^2$ to the absolute norm — so the log-vector lands in the codimension-1 hyperplane $\\sum x_i=0$."
