            "answer": 2,
            "explain": "$\\ell(u)=0$ means $|\\sigma_i(u)|=1$ for every archimedean place. Such an algebraic integer with all conjugates on the unit circle is a root of unity by Kronecker's theorem. Conversely every root of unity has all conjugates of absolute value $1$, so $\\ker\\ell=\\mu_K$, which is finite (it's a finite subgroup of $K^\\times$, hence cyclic)."
