            "answer": 0.5,
            "tol": 0.001,
            "explain": "The functional equation is $\\Lambda(s,f)=\\pm\\Lambda(1-s,f)$, fixing the center at $s=1/2$. This is the same line on which the Eisenstein continuous spectrum lives — not a coincidence, since the Mellin transform of the Whittaker model produces $\\Lambda(s,f)$."
