            "answer": 1,
            "explain": "$\\deg K_C = 2g - 2$. For $g = 0$, $\\deg K_C = -2 < 0$ so all powers have no sections and $\\kappa = -\\infty$. For $g = 1$, $K_C \\cong \\mathcal{O}_C$ so $h^0(K_C^{\\otimes m}) = 1$ for every $m \\ge 0$ — constant growth gives $\\kappa = 0$. For $g \\ge 2$, $K_C$ is ample of degree $2g-2$, and Riemann–Roch gives $h^0(K_C^{\\otimes m}) = (2g-2)m - g + 1$ for $m \\ge 2$, linear growth so $\\kappa = 1 = \\dim C$.",
