            "type": "numeric",
            "q": "A term of $\\Sigma_{n:\\mathbb{N}} \\mathsf{Vec}(\\mathbb{R},n)$ is a pair $(n,v)$ with $v$ a vector of length $n$. If we project the second component of $(3,(1.0,2.0,3.0))$, how many real entries does the resulting vector have?",
            "answer": 3,
